  <p>These Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your use of the <a href="https://journeysbyjaz.com">journeysbyjaz.com</a> website and the vacation planning services of <strong>Journeys by Jaz</strong> (“Journeys by Jaz,” “we,” “us” or “our”). By using our website or requesting our services, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the website or services. Our <a href="./privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> is part of these Terms.</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are and what we do</h2>
  <p>Journeys by Jaz is an independent travel advisor and vacation planner. We research and recommend travel options, such as theme-park vacations, cruises, all-inclusive resorts and group trips, and help you book them. We are affiliated with Enchanted Escapes Travel (Enchanted Escapes, LLC), an Authorized Disney Vacation Planner agency in Cypress, Texas, through which bookings are made. Florida Seller of Travel #ST40359.</p>
  <p><strong>We are not the supplier of your travel.</strong> Airlines, cruise lines, resorts, hotels, parks, tour operators and other suppliers provide the travel services you purchase. Their own terms, conditions and policies apply to those services.</p>

  <h2>2. Planning fee</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Our planning service has a flat fee of <strong>$35</strong>, which is separate from the cost of your travel.</li>
    <li>Once we receive your signed service agreement, the planning fee and your trip details, we will send you 2–3 custom vacation options, normally within 3 days. Delivery time may vary during very busy periods or if we need more information from you.</li>
    <li><strong>The planning fee is non-refundable.</strong> It covers our time spent on research, consultation and itinerary building, whether or not you decide to book.</li>
    <li>Please read the service agreement before you pay. If this page and your service agreement differ, the service agreement controls for your engagement with us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Bookings and payments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>After you choose an option, you complete a secure booking form with Enchanted Escapes Travel. We then book the travel for you.</li>
    <li><strong>Your travel payments go directly to the supplier</strong> (for example, Disney, the cruise line or the resort). Your card is charged by the supplier, which can take up to 48 hours. Enchanted Escapes Travel does not charge your card.</li>
    <li>You may be able to pay a deposit, or a deposit plus remaining payments by the supplier’s due dates. You are responsible for making payments on time. Late or missed payments may result in cancellation by the supplier and loss of deposits.</li>
    <li>A booking is confirmed only when the supplier confirms it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Prices, availability and quotes</h2>
  <p>Resorts, parks and cruise lines set their own prices, and prices, fees, taxes, itineraries and availability are subject to change without notice until your booking is confirmed and paid as required by the supplier. We do not guarantee that booking through us will be cheaper than booking directly. Quotes we provide are estimates based on information available when they are prepared. We will show what is included and what costs extra so you can compare, but you should review all supplier details before booking.</p>

  <h2>5. Changes and cancellations</h2>
  <p>Supplier cancellation, change and refund policies apply to your travel and may include penalties or no refund. Please review them before you book. If you need to change or cancel, contact us as soon as possible and we will help you where we can, but we cannot override a supplier’s policies. Our planning fee is not refundable (see Section 2).</p>

  <h2>6. Travel insurance</h2>
  <p>We can provide a travel insurance quote so you can decide whether to protect your trip. Insurance is optional, is provided by third-party insurers under their own terms, and may not cover every situation. Some coverage options must be purchased within a limited time after your first trip payment. You are responsible for reading the policy and deciding whether to buy it.</p>

  <h2>7. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give us accurate and complete information, including traveler names exactly as they appear on identification, dates of birth, and contact details.</li>
    <li>Make sure every traveler has valid travel documents (such as passports, visas, and any required health documents) and meets age, health, vaccination and entry requirements. Government and supplier requirements can change, and we are not responsible for denied boarding or entry caused by missing or invalid documents.</li>
    <li>Review confirmations and itineraries carefully and tell us right away if anything is wrong.</li>
    <li>Follow the supplier’s rules, safety instructions and codes of conduct.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Travel risks</h2>
  <p>Travel involves risks, including weather, delays, cancellations, schedule or itinerary changes, illness, accidents, strikes, political or security events, and other events outside our control. You choose to travel at your own risk. We do not control and are not responsible for the services or conduct of suppliers or third parties.</p>

